# tally 2.1.8 P50, E §4.1, §10 (the last review input, k9k10): an explain of a balance lists the movements of one day
# with their keys in index order, never as text: at the window's end 2026-03-25 save[k9] comes before save[k10], as
# on its first day. 00a00b22 listed save[k10] first there. tally 2.2 (2.2-3): the two readings, `after save[k9]` and
# `after save[k10]`, are stated at the window's end, 2026-03-25 end, so they anchor there and the explain starts from
# konto's reading.
# tally 2.2.1 (#218, E §4.2 step 4): the window has ended before 2026-03-25's closing readings, so the anchors state
# konto and sav there and after: b and e are values, and the explain from the anchor lists no movement.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-06-10
  start 2026-03-01
  end 2026-06-30

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
index ks = [k9, k10]
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place sav: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input d_save: date
input amt: money PLN

move save[k in ks]: transfers
  on d_save
  reads konto
  leg cash from konto to sav amount min(amt, bal(konto))

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  amt = 10.00 PLN "s"
  d_save = window(2026-03-16, 2026-03-25) "s"
  opening[konto] = 1000.00 PLN at 2026-03-01 start "s"
  opening[sav] = 0.00 PLN at 2026-03-01 start "s"

version r
  cite s
  governs 2026-03
  known 2026-04-02
  covers konto, sav
  anchor konto
  anchor sav
  stated[konto] = 700.00 PLN at 2026-03-25 end "after k9"
  stated[sav] = 25.00 PLN at 2026-03-25 end "after k10"

ask b: bal(konto, 2026-03-25), bal(konto, 2026-03-31), bal(sav, 2026-03-31)
ask e: explain bal(konto, 2026-03-31)
ask l: last(stated[konto], 2026-03-31)
=== expect
b: (700.00 PLN, 700.00 PLN, 25.00 PLN)
  anchor: konto 2026-03-25 end, stated 700.00 PLN, difference ?"date within window(2026-03-16, 2026-03-25) not precise enough for the day of save[k10]" (save[k10]) ?"date within window(2026-03-16, 2026-03-25) not precise enough for the day of save[k9]" (save[k9])
  anchor: sav 2026-03-25 end, stated 25.00 PLN, difference ?"date within window(2026-03-16, 2026-03-25) not precise enough for the day of save[k10]" (save[k10]) ?"date within window(2026-03-16, 2026-03-25) not precise enough for the day of save[k9]" (save[k9])
  cut 2026-06-10
e: 700.00 PLN
  balance of konto (PLN) at the end of 2026-03-31
  from: anchor r:stated[konto] = 700.00 PLN, 2026-03-25 end (version r, source s, locator "after k9"), gap role anchor, gap ?"date within window(2026-03-16, 2026-03-25) not precise enough for the day of save[k10]" (save[k10]) ?"date within window(2026-03-16, 2026-03-25) not precise enough for the day of save[k9]" (save[k9])
  no movement
  anchor: konto 2026-03-25 end, stated 700.00 PLN, difference ?"date within window(2026-03-16, 2026-03-25) not precise enough for the day of save[k10]" (save[k10]) ?"date within window(2026-03-16, 2026-03-25) not precise enough for the day of save[k9]" (save[k9])
  cut 2026-06-10
l: 700.00 PLN
  held: stated[konto] = 700.00 PLN (r), read for 2026-03-31
  cut 2026-06-10
warning: WARN-UNREAD place world is read by nothing
